I need a getter `eyePos` that returns the world position of the eyes, using a constant eye height (1.55 meters) scaled by the current model scale (so crouching works). For network updates, `pushState(msg)` will push a snapshot containing timestamp, position (msg.p[0], msg.p[1]), yaw, crouch flag, and movement flag. Keep the buffer trimmed to a reasonable length (20).

